| `KEEL_GATE_RUN_DATE` | string; dynamic | unset: the local clock; `scripts/gate_evidence.py` sets it for every goal it runs | a calendar date written `YYYY-MM-DD`, no later than the clock and at most `config/project.json` `evidence.run_date.max_age_days` (`1`) days before it | `scripts/run_date.py`, for `scripts/gate_evidence.py` and `scripts/jobs/review_docs.py` | Sets the date the doc review and the restamper call today when neither `--today` nor `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` is given, so every check of one `make verify` judges by the day the run began. `config/project.json` `evidence.run_date.env` names it and `child_env.names` lists it. A value that fails the rule is refused with exit 2. | pinning a reproducible build's date: `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` | always |
